{ % vim: set ft=djot : % }

# djotls

[![codecov](
https://codecov.io/gh/black-desk/djotls/graph/badge.svg?token=GF5SAU9WIC
)](https://codecov.io/gh/black-desk/djotls)

::: warning

{*This project is under very early stage and not ready for use.*}

:::

djotls is a [`Djot`](https://djot.net) toolkit written in Rust, with a
parser,
formatter (`djotfmt`) and language server (`djotls`).

## Build

``` bash
cargo build --release
```

## Test

``` bash
cargo test --release
```

## Install

``` bash
cargo install --path .
```

## Usage

You can check the usage by running:

``` bash
cargo run -r -- --help
```

Or after installing:

``` bash
djotfmt --help
djotls --help
```

## Language server

The `djotls` executable provides formatting, navigation, references,
heading outlines, completion and diagnostics over stdio.
See the [language server guide](docs/lsp.md) for setup and scope.

